  ],
  cyberpunk: [
    {
      question: "Why is Discord Dark Mode the best backdrop for cyberpunk banners?",
      answer: "Discord's default client interface is dark mode (#313338), which means neon cyan (#00F0FF), hot magenta (#FF0055), and electric violet (#8B5CF6) pop with maximum luminance. By configuring your Discord profile hex to an obsidian black (such as #090C16), the perimeter of your banner merges seamlessly into the dark UI."
    },
    {
      question: "How do holographic scanlines and cyber grid animations render on mobile Discord?",
      answer: "Mobile Discord scales profile banners down while retaining the 16:9 aspect ratio. Fine scanlines can sometimes moiré if drawn too thin. Our cyberpunk motion presets use bold 2px–3px grid lines and rhythmic glow sweeps that stay crisp and artifact-free across iPhone, Android, and 4K desktop displays."
    },
    {
      question: "What are the safe-zone rules for cyberpunk HUD and terminal banners?",
      answer: "Cyberpunk HUD elements often run along the borders of the graphic. Keep critical interface readouts at least 48px below the top border (away from status badges) and at least 140px away from the bottom-left corner to accommodate the circular profile picture cutout."
